 "text": "Hello, how are things going? In general, yes. A wide angle that helps see little things on the screen is worth paying for. How often do you use one leg on a computer? Then a nice wide that lets you see the whole screen at once is worth its weight in gold. A good wide also performs basic photo editing. You can, but you'll lose the main benefit of having it on the screen. If you only need it for basic editing, an external is fine. Then a low profile camera that turns on a dime is worth considering. Many cheap webcams are basically tiny cameras that weren't designed with use as a web cam in mind.",
